; Entity handler: water drop hanging from a stalactite (kind 9, rooms 15 and 19)
;
; The cyan drops that form at the tip of the stalactites of Gloomy tunnels (room 15) and Underground river (room 19), swell
; and fall. A drop cycles through two handlers: this one while it hangs and #R$B534 while it falls. Entered with SP
; at slot+2, see #R$B2A6 for the stack scheme. Slot fields used: +4 byte y of the stalactite tip, +7 byte x, +$B
; byte start delay; the whole layout is at #R$B56D.
; .
; The start delay (byte +$B, the fifth parameter of the room record: $0B-$3D frames, so that the drops of a room do
; not fall together) is decremented each frame and written back while it is nonzero; the drop is neither drawn nor
; tested until it reaches 0. From then on it stays 1 (the decrement leaves 0 and the zero is not stored) and each
; frame the drop is placed at the tip (x/4, y of the tip) and drawn with a single draw command (IY = #R$B407, the hanging
; drop of the sprite description), without a hit box test (the two hit box words +$C..+$F are skipped), and
; #R$B56D counts the animation down.
; .
; Hardware: none.
;
; SP Slot address + 2
@label=UpdateDropHanging
c$B512 POP BC        ; skip the speed
 $B513 POP DE        ; E = y of the tip, D = y where the fall ends
 $B514 POP HL        ; H = x
 $B515 LD D,H        ; D = x
 $B516 POP HL        ; skip y
 $B517 POP AF        ; A = start delay
 $B518 DEC A         ;
 $B519 JR Z,$B523    ; over: draw the drop
 $B51B PUSH AF       ; store the decremented delay
@isub=LD HL,SLOT_SIZE-$A
 $B51C LD HL,$000C   ; SP is slot+$A: not drawn, next slot
 $B51F ADD HL,SP     ;
 $B520 JP $A5F0      ; #R$A5F0 enters the handler of the slot at HL
*$B523 LD H,D        ; H = x
 $B524 LD L,E        ; L = y of the tip
 $B525 SRA H         ; x / 4: byte column
 $B527 SRA H         ;
 $B529 LD ($ACD3),HL ; draw command position: (y, x/4)
 $B52C POP HL        ; skip the hit box
 $B52D POP HL        ;
 $B52E LD IY,$B407   ; queue one draw command
 $B532 JR $B56D      ; animate and queue
